The provided code snippet is a method named `makeValidCdmObjectName` that takes a string `name` as input and returns a new string with the following modifications:

1. Trims any leading or trailing whitespace from the input string.
2. Checks if the string contains any non-alphanumeric characters (excluding spaces).
3. If the string contains any non-alphanumeric characters, it replaces them with spaces.
4. Returns the modified string.

Here is a summary of the code:

```java
public static String makeValidCdmObjectName(String name) {
    // Trim leading and trailing whitespace
    name = name.trim();

    // Check if the string contains any non-alphanumeric characters (excluding spaces)
    boolean ok = true;
    for (int i = 0; i < name.length(); i++) {
        int c = name.charAt(i);
        if (c < 0x20) ok = false;
        if (c == ' ') ok = false;
        if (c == ' ') ok = false;
        if (!ok) break;
    }

    if (ok) {
        return name;
    }

    // Replace non-alphanumeric characters with spaces
    StringBuilder sbuff = new StringBuilder(name.length());
    for (int i = 0, len = name.length(); i < len; i++) {
        int c = name.charAt(i);
        if ((c == ' ') || (c == ' ')) sbuff.append(' ');
        else if (c >= 0x20) sbuff.append((char)c);
    }

    return sbuff.toString();
}
```

